// TEST: A scalar beside an array of another element is not lifted (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999 @ 8:26
// ERROR-CONTAINS: must agree EXACTLY
// `add0(A, s)` lifts the scalar over the array (arity/036). With an Int64
// scalar beside Float64 elements the lift used to retype the kernel and
// refuse at the array's first element ("expected Int64, got Float64"); the
// lift declines and the call is refused at the disagreeing argument.
function add0(a: T^0, b: T^0) -> T^0 = a + b
let a = add0([0.5, 0.5], 1)
